WEBVTT

00:03:27.371 --> 00:03:30.448
And this realization is allowing
us to re-conceptualize

00:03:30.472 --> 00:03:32.884
the way that we actually
approach these diseases,

00:03:32.908 --> 00:03:34.892
by controlling angiogenesis.

00:03:35.829 --> 00:03:37.738
Now, I'm going to focus on cancer,

00:03:37.762 --> 00:03:41.229
because angiogenesis
is a hallmark of cancer --

00:03:41.253 --> 00:03:42.681
every type of cancer.

00:03:43.253 --> 00:03:44.407
So here we go.

00:03:44.946 --> 00:03:48.836
This is a tumor: dark, gray, ominous
mass growing inside a brain.

00:03:48.860 --> 00:03:50.109
And under the microscope,

00:03:50.133 --> 00:03:53.146
you can see hundreds
of these brown-stained blood vessels,

00:03:53.170 --> 00:03:55.217
capillaries that are feeding cancer cells,

00:03:55.241 --> 00:03:57.194
bringing oxygen and nutrients.

00:03:58.289 --> 00:04:00.368
But cancers don't start out like this,